# The optional "public front door": gives Home a real https:// address that
# works from anywhere (a work PC, a phone on mobile data). Only started when
# you ask for it — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "A permanent address from
# anywhere". Not used at all for a plain home-LAN setup.
#
# {$HOME_DOMAIN} is read from the root .env file (e.g. myhome.duckdns.org).
# Caddy sees that name, proves to Let's Encrypt that this server really is
# that address, and then fetches AND renews the HTTPS certificate on its own.
# For that to work the name must already point at this server, and ports 80
# and 443 must be reachable from the internet.
{$HOME_DOMAIN} {
	# Everything goes to the existing gateway, which routes to each app
	# exactly as it does on the LAN. Caddy adds the visitor's real address
	# (X-Forwarded-For) itself, and streams large uploads and videos
	# straight through without buffering them.
	reverse_proxy gateway:80
}
